## Why This Is Asked
Tests an asynchronous, idempotent flow common in payments; exercises end-to-end behavior, including 202 semantics, Location header, polling, and fault tolerance.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys prevent duplicate side effects
- Asynchronous processing and status polling
- Proper error handling for missing/invalid headers
- Downstream failure resilience with preserved idempotency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Jest-like sketch
test('idempotent POST /payments', async () => {
  const key = 'idem-123';
  const r1 = await post('/payments', { amount: 100 }, { 'Idempotency-Key': key });
  const r2 = await post('/payments', { amount: 100 }, { 'Idempotency-Key': key });
  expect(r1.status).toBe(202);
  expect(r1.headers.Location).toContain('/payments/');
  expect(r2.status).toBe(202);
  expect(r2.body.id).toBe(r1.body.id);
  // poll until final state
  const id = r1.body.id;
  let s = await get(`/payments/${id}/status`);
  while (s.state === 'pending') s = await get(`/payments/${id}/status`);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend tests for long-running payments and timeouts?
- How would you test idempotency across multiple regions or microservices?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for high-concurrency, real-time messaging with ordering and durability are common in collaboration apps. This question probes ability to design end-to-end tests that cover connection scalability, in-order delivery, offline replay, backpressure, and resilience to broker outages.

## Key Concepts

- WebSocket load testing and client choreography
- In-order delivery guarantees with per-room sequencing
- Durable stores for replay (Redis Streams, Kafka, or similar)
- Backpressure handling and reconnection logic
- Failure modes: partial broker outages, network partitions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test sketch for sequencing validation
let roomId = 'room-42';
let lastSeq = 0;
ws.onmessage = (evt) => {
  const msg = JSON.parse(evt.data);
  if (msg.roomId === roomId) {
    if (msg.seq <= lastSeq) fail('out-of-order');
    lastSeq = msg.seq;
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure end-to-end latency under peak load and under broker outage?
- What tooling would you use to generate 10k concurrent connections and validate ordering?
